==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|life|en- -en}} {{q|intensifying verbal [[circumfix]]}}.<ref name="OED-etym"> The '''Oxford English Dictionary''' (2007) states that '''enliven''' was formed by the simultaneous prefixing of {{m|en|en-}} and suffixing of {{m|en|-en}}, which, by definition, constitutes [[circumfix]]ation.</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ɛnˈlaɪvən/}}
*: {{rhymes|en|aɪvən|s=3}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-enliven.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|archaic|transitive}} To give [[life]] or [[spirit]] to; to [[revive]] or [[animate]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make more [[lively]], [[cheerful]] or [[interesting]].
#: ''The game was much '''enlivened''' when both teams scored within five minutes of each other.''

